     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day is about five times the maximum daily dose. No indication I know of supports it, and it carries a serious risk of life-threatening lactic acidosis. A single 4250 mg dose is also over four times the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can do that right away, for example 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, or a lower starting dose such as 500 mg twice daily.\n- **Discuss it with your attending and pharmacy.** If you think there's a reason for an off-label dose, they can review it and co-sign. Many hospital systems require that for doses this far outside the limits.\n- **Check for a typo.** If the dose was meant to be 425 mg or 850 mg, tell me and I'll enter it.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
